Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 17:07:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 044/154] refactor: the controller compiles as C++
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ControllerForNSWindow was the last AppKit name in the header, and the only
call the 3883-line controller made into an Objective-C returning method. It
now takes gfx::NativeWindow - a plain C++ class on macOS wrapping the NSWindow
- and compares against window()->GetNativeWindow() rather than
GetNSWindowForAnimation(). The header names no AppKit type at all, so its
__OBJC__ fork and the two NSWindow forward declarations are gone.

Five call sites in the dispatcher delegate wrap the NSWindow the key event
landed on. The peek widget stops unwrapping a gfx::NativeWindow it already
held, which is one call shorter than before.

The file is now .cc. Verified by the object file rebuilding and by the built
libchrome_dll.dylib carrying the new log string and none of the old one.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
index 636e4df200e93..f4cfb99ca6b2d 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
@@ -3503,7 +3503,7 @@ static_library("ui") {
   if (is_mac) {
     sources += [
       "atrium/atrium_browser_controller.h",
-      "atrium/atrium_browser_controller.mm",
+      "atrium/atrium_browser_controller.cc",
       "atrium/atrium_browser_window.h",
       "atrium/atrium_browser_window.mm",
       "atrium/atrium_capture.h",
